content:
Chargeback fee money returned to a seller on a won card chargeback case is booked on the Northloop Payments ledger as a fee-return entry on that case.

## Situation of use and capability

`return_won_chargeback_fee_5c062853` returns chargeback fee money on a chargeback case to a seller's Northloop Payments account. One call books one chargeback reversal entry of the fee-return kind on the payments ledger for the chargeback case named, and raises the account's total balance by the amount returned; the seller then sees the returned fee against that chargeback case in their payments history. The amount is taken exactly as given; nothing else on the account or the case changes.

## How it is invoked

This is an agent-side tool: the support agent unlocks `return_won_chargeback_fee_5c062853` and then calls it.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `payout_account_id` | the payments account reference number of the seller's Northloop Payments account, as returned by the payments account lookup | identifier |
| `chargeback_case_id` | the chargeback case reference number the fee is returned on, as shown on the chargeback dispute lookup and on the chargeback fee in the payments ledger | identifier |
| `amount` | the fee amount returned, in USD | a positive number with 2 decimal places (cents), rounded to the cent before it is passed; booked exactly as given |

## Return

A text rendering of a dictionary describing the entry booked:

- `status` — the literal `fee_returned` when the entry was booked;
- `payout_event_id` — reference of the new payments ledger entry;
- `chargeback_case_id` — the chargeback case the fee was returned on;
- `fee_movement` — the literal `fee_returned`;
- `amount` — the amount returned in USD with 2 decimal places;
- `balance` — the account's total balance in USD after the return, 2 decimal places;
- `event_date` — the date of the return, YYYY-MM-DD.
